# Controller & route comment format

When creating or modifying controller functions (and route handlers when documented at the route layer), add a JSDoc block **directly above** the exported handler using this exact format:

```typescript
/**
 * @Description [Brief description of what the handler does]
 * @Route [HTTP_METHOD] [Full route path including /api prefix if mounted]
 * @Access [Public | Private]
 */
```

Match existing controllers (e.g. booking): use the real mounted path such as `POST /api/booking/book-companion/:id`, not only the router-relative segment.
